From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yevhen Salitrynskyi <ysalitrynskyi@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 22:53:27 -0400
Subject: feat: a drag takes a tab into the essentials and out (issue 16)

As in Arc (pins H27; BACKLOG S-277, S-289, GitHub issue 16): a tab's row
dragged over the essentials, or the room above the Space's title down to
the list from the sidebar's top row, turns into a card under the pointer,
the size of the place it would take, while the cards part to make that
place and the list closes up over the row; released there it settles into
the place and becomes an essential, before the card after it or after the
last. An essential's card dragged onto the list turns into a row under the
pointer, in line with the rows, while the rows part where it would land
and the grid keeps its height; released there it settles into the room
and stops being an essential, at that place: under the Clear line a tab,
over it a pin of the Space. Dragged back, the copy turns back into the row
or card and fades over it. It had taken the tab's menu.

The drop decides, as a drop across the Clear line does (pins H14), and
nothing is pinned or unpinned during the drag: a pin change remakes the
tab's view in the other container, which the drag still holds.
TabDragHandlerImpl keeps the pointer's last place and shows the floating
copy (EssentialsDragGhost, on the sidebar region, over both scroll views);
the row or card it stands in for keeps its bounds and the drag's events,
drawn at no opacity (kHiddenForEssentialsDrag, which the animating layout
manager keeps), and its container closes up over it.
PinnedTabContainerView makes room for cards at an index and says which
place a pointer is nearest; UnpinnedTabContainerView makes room for rows
before a row, over or under the Clear line, and reads a drop's place from
the rows as they would stand without the room. The copy turns, settles
and fades only while Stedding animates (motion O1).

Tests: PinnedRunTest.ADragTakesATabIntoTheEssentialsAndOut,
PinnedRunTest.ADraggedTabTurnsIntoACardAndBack.

Why: Arc users move tabs into and out of their Favorites by dragging, and
asked for it, then for Arc's way of showing it (GitHub issue 16).
Removable when: never; it is product behaviour.
